1
00:00:00,351 --> 00:00:03,501
Every insurer publishes a list of doctors

2
00:00:03,501 --> 00:00:04,724
Most of it is wrong

3
00:00:04,724 --> 00:00:07,169
and by law someone has to phone every

4
00:00:07,169 --> 00:00:08,379
office to fix it

5
00:00:08,848 --> 00:00:10,493
Rollcall makes the calls

6
00:00:11,544 --> 00:00:13,331
Senate staff phoned a hundred

7
00:00:13,331 --> 00:00:15,269
and twenty listed therapists

8
00:00:15,269 --> 00:00:17,377
They could book an appointment eighteen

9
00:00:17,377 --> 00:00:18,544
percent of the time

10
00:00:18,544 --> 00:00:20,704
Retired, moved, wrong number

11
00:00:20,704 --> 00:00:22,451
not taking that plan

12
00:00:23,618 --> 00:00:26,168
Nobody chooses to make these calls

13
00:00:26,168 --> 00:00:28,023
Three US rules require them

14
00:00:28,023 --> 00:00:29,556
from every health plan

15
00:00:29,556 --> 00:00:31,260
every ninety days

16
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:32,461
Meet Rollcall

17
00:00:32,461 --> 00:00:34,736
Forty listings, unchecked for a year

18
00:00:34,736 --> 00:00:35,547
One click

19
00:00:35,995 --> 00:00:39,146
Six lines dial six offices at once

20
00:00:39,146 --> 00:00:41,315
Each call checks five things

21
00:00:41,315 --> 00:00:42,760
still here, address

22
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:44,206
phone, new patients

23
00:00:44,206 --> 00:00:45,355
in network

24
00:00:45,355 --> 00:00:47,855
Every clear answer lands in its cell

25
00:00:47,855 --> 00:00:50,881
A correction shows the old value struck through

26
00:00:50,881 --> 00:00:53,523
A retired doctor gets flagged for removal

27
00:00:53,998 --> 00:00:55,150
Forty calls later

28
00:00:55,150 --> 00:00:56,606
